From d89bdb8766b3b4b183eec56bb22da668a975bda7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:20:24 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] kcm_kwinxwayland: one FormLayout page, hint labels
 under choices, app list on a lazy sub-page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (+ List sub-page). Config keys, kcfg, defaults and the logout helper unchanged. NOT BUILT YET.

Moved / renamed:
- Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry (subtitle per entry) replaced by Kirigami.FormLayout with the same radio texts; each
  subtitle is now a small wrapping hint label under its choice. The intro paragraph above the page is now a
  ContextualHelpButton next to the first choice. Groups are separated by section separators; labels unchanged.
- The allowed/denied list page moved from an invisible ScrollViewKCM nested in the main ColumnLayout to ui/AppsPage.qml,
  opened with kcm.push("AppsPage.qml", {setting, title}); empty list shows a PlaceholderMessage; remove button got
  Accessible.name. "See Allowed/Denied Applications…" now sit under the choice they belong to.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-023, HIG-057. page-design.md 1, 2, 3, 7.

Speed cause (code evidence): the old main.qml instantiated the whole ScrollViewKCM + ListView (model
kcm.settings[""] with an unset name) inside the page at startup, and used the heavy Kirigami.Form with four
FormGroups; C++ constructor only registers settings (kcmkwinxwayland.cpp:25-31). Now only the form is built on open and
the list when pushed. After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet. Unconfirmed: Layout.maximumWidth on
hint labels inside FormLayout (same recipe as plasma-desktop 56095d1); ContextualHelpButton inside a RowLayout row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
